Padding-invariance patch for unimol_tools 0.1.5 (Uni-Mol v2 models).

Stock unimol_tools lets padded atoms leak into real ones in three places, so a
molecule's embedding depends on the largest molecule in its batch (max abs
shift ~1e2 on the 1.1B model, comparable to the difference between two
molecules):
  1. models/unimolv2.py      attention mask is all zeros -> padded keys take softmax mass
  2. models/transformersv2.py outer-product scale uses the padded length N_pad;
                              with the output bias a real pair gets (W o + N_pad b)/(1 + 1e-3 N_pad)
  3. models/transformersv2.py triangle multiplication scale uses N_pad
Each hunk reduces to the stock computation when nothing is padded, so
single-molecule results are bit-identical. PADDING_INVARIANT marks a patched
install; equiflex.prep.featurize.UniMolExtractor refuses to run without it.

Apply / revert / verify with scripts/patch_unimol.sh.

--- a/models/unimolv2.py
+++ b/models/unimolv2.py
@@ -235,6 +235,13 @@
         x = x.type(dtype)
 
         attn_mask = attn_bias.clone()
+        # equiflex padding patch: exclude padded atoms (atom_mask == 0) from
+        # attention. Column 0 is the CLS token and is always a valid key, so no
+        # query row is entirely -inf.
+        pad_keys = torch.cat(
+            [torch.zeros_like(atom_mask[:, :1]), atom_mask == 0], dim=1
+        ).bool()
+        attn_mask = attn_mask.masked_fill(pad_keys.unsqueeze(1), float('-inf'))
         attn_bias = torch.zeros_like(attn_mask)
         attn_mask = attn_mask.unsqueeze(1).repeat(
             1, self.args.encoder_attention_heads, 1, 1
